  "repeats": [],
  "notes": [
   "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
   "The common-anode RGB LED sits in neighbouring columns 10-13 of row a, in the catalogue order R, COM, G, B. The COM (longest) leg is the second leg, as the text says.",
   "Wire from 5V goes to the LED's COM strip (column 11, top half). The text says the 5V wire goes to the longest pin.",
   "Each LED cathode leg (R, G, B) has its own 220 ohm resistor. The resistor crosses the centre gap to the bottom half of the same column. A jumper wire then runs from the Arduino pin (R to 3, G to 5, B to 6) to that bottom-half strip.",
   "Resistors are on the cathode side, as in the image. Exact breadboard columns are chosen, since the image is only a partial view."
  ]
 },
